## Statement

Prove that $\sqrt{2}$ is irrational.

## Hint

Assume $\sqrt{2}=p/q$ with $p,q$ coprime integers, then look at the parity of $p$ and $q$.

## Solution

Suppose $\sqrt2=\dfrac pq$ with $p,q\in\mathbb{N}^*$ coprime.

Then $p^2=2q^2$, so $p^2$ is even, hence $p$ is even: $p=2k$. Substituting gives $4k^2=2q^2$, that is $q^2=2k^2$, so $q$ is even too.

Both $p$ and $q$ are divisible by 2, which contradicts coprimality. Therefore $\sqrt2\notin\mathbb{Q}$.
